{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency","id":165354,"title":"Monster of the Week Exigency","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-10T16:59:36-07:00","id":165354,"title":"Monster of the Week Exigency","content":"You know what I kinda want to see?<br /> <br /> Exigencies from Forbidden Gods and/or Gods of Atrocity; with all their charms focused on making you a big honkin' <i>monster</i>.<br /> <br /> I want them to have the following traits:<ul><li>They give you a big ol' boost of power.</li> <li>They make you really inhuman.</li> <li>They pare away at your options until killing everybody seems like the only reasonable, sane solution.</li> </ul><br /> I don't want this for <i>players</i>, exactly; I want this as something I can have Gods of Atrocity just toss out there, secure in the knowledge that they will inevitably decay into a self-sustaining cycle of violence and despair.<br /> <br /> Because... it just feels like something that would exist, ya know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T17:31:53-07:00","id":165426,"title":"","content":"Don't let Vance see this, it comes a little too close to being the perfect villain for his Magical Girl Shard!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T18:04:40-07:00","id":165456,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a good way to have an action-oriented campaign in a small area. PCs are leading peaceful, normal lives? Oh no! The evil King Shaitaan has unleashed a monster on the unsuspecting populace! If only there were a circle of solar heroes who could save them...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T18:07:39-07:00","id":165457,"title":"","content":"isnt that something like the black market exigent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T18:18:45-07:00","id":165461,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd really like to see this. A lot of people complained that Infernals (especially pre-Crane) were locked into a specific arc on the basis of their primary Yozi, but with Exigents that's actually totally fine, since they don't need to support a wide range of concepts.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have an idea for a thermonuclear death-spiral Exigent of Adamant (probably a black-market attempt to gin up the Ultimate Most Powerful Exalt) who is basically Phoenix from X-men. The character arc is around building rapidly in power but also losing control as you do so. Some of my loose notions so far:<ul><li>The character's Essence increases by one dot every time she Limit Breaks, and she has some charms that can accelerate this process in order to lend her power when acting passionately. Anything that would cause her permanent Essence to go down fails. At Essence 10, either she goes permanently out of control and becomes an adversary NPC, or she explodes violently and transmutes a huge area to glass, or she evaporates into pure energy and leaves her heart behind as a five-dot Hearthstone that does not require a manse or demesne (ST's choice).</li> <li>Her powers kind of suck and her mote pool is low compared to others of equal Essence, so she's really underwhelming early on, but can outpace anyone else in the long haul just because she can easily end up 4-5 Essence above every other PC.</li> <li>She uses Attribute charms, <i>sort of</i> -- the Trait prerequisites are of the form (Attribute + Essence), ranging from 3 to 10. Dice-adder cap is also Attribute + Essence, maximum 10. The upshot of this is that as you reach the upper echelons of power, your abilities become less distinctive and less about who you are as a person, because you start bumping into the cap. Powers near the prereq cap tend to be a bit creepy and over-the-top and express the nature of the Exaltation rather than the nature of the character.</li> <li>On any turn in which she spends motes (or any 5-second period, outside of combat), she must spend at least (Essence) motes or the difference is spent automatically as a surcharge.</li> <li>In general, her higher-essence powers are harder to control, and she has a lot of effects that are harder to control specifically as Essence increases</li> <li>Her bonfire anima tends to coat things with a brittle, paper-thin layer of glass, and causes thin needles of glass to sprout randomly from surfaces.</li> </ul><br /> It's a hilariously disruptive concept, so I can't imagine it'd work well as a PC in most groups, but it's kind of implicit that at some point you'll melt down and retire the PC, and the focus shifts on the other PCs' efforts to clean up the mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 06-10-2014, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T00:16:34-07:00","id":165700,"title":"","content":"hmmm....this could be an interesting use of Exigency. I honestly don't want yet another PC splat thrown into the mix...I feel that field is crowded enough already. But utilizing Exigents as potential antagonists has some potential I think...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T01:40:52-07:00","id":165733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=165700#post165700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmm....this could be an interesting use of Exigency. I honestly don't want yet another PC splat thrown into the mix...I feel that field is crowded enough already. But utilizing Exigents as potential antagonists has some potential I think...</div> </div> </div> </div>You're free to use Exigents this way, but the books presenting them as solely antagonist material would be needlessly limiting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T02:24:41-07:00","id":165741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=165461#post165461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some cool stuff about Jean Grey</div> </div> </div> </div>One possible idea would be that the 5 dot &quot;free&quot; hearthstone (more like a heartstone in this case <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) is in fact the exaltation, and will &quot;enter&quot; any suitable host who uses it.<br /> This would be good way of bringing the whole &quot;phoenix rises from ashes&quot; angle to life, and could also have a few narrative hooks : the young peasant girl that grew up with one of the PCs used the heartstone and was deemed worthy by the exaltation. The PCs know (from previous experience or previous existance) that such Exalted are doomed and destined to cause great harm around them as they flare up - how will they all deal with it ?...<br /> <br /> Nice concept in all cases.<br /> I must say Solars are my favourite Exalts of all (I know, they feel vanilla and stuff, but the concept of mythical heroes of old is a really powerful draw to me...), but I really liked Janest, and Exigents also (note: also, not only) are a good way of introducing challenging foes that are a bit less &quot;archetypical&quot; than Dusk Deathknights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1609-fumble","name":"Fumble","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T08:44:21-07:00","id":165961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=165733#post165733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're free to use Exigents this way, but the books presenting them as solely antagonist material would be needlessly limiting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> oh, of course.<br /> <br /> I feel the same way about Infernals as well. They should be limited to NPC antagonists. But that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T09:08:10-07:00","id":165981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=165461#post165461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea for a thermonuclear death-spiral Exigent of Adamant (probably a black-market attempt to gin up the Ultimate Most Powerful Exalt) who is basically Phoenix from X-men. The character arc is around building rapidly in power but also losing control as you do so. Some of my loose notions so far:</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me a lot of the False Awakening from nWoD Mage, though that was a deliberate parody of Mary Sue archetypes. In case you're not aware:<br /> <br /> The False Awakening starts with someone seemingly Awakening to a Watchtower from a Supernal Realm no one's ever heard of before, with a combination of Favored Arcana that never existed before. This person rapidly grows in power, gaining a dot in Gnosis <i>every week</i>, until they finally reach Gnosis 10 and EXPLODE, taking out a city block with them. In reality, the False Awakening is an Abyssal intruder that spreads from one target to another, but needs to be constantly hunted down lest they do some <i>real</i> damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T09:09:55-07:00","id":165983,"title":"","content":"If you provide stats for the thing, people will play as the thing. If you do not provide stats for the thing, people will make up their own stats and play as the thing anyway. This &quot;limited to NPC&quot; concept is strange and confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T10:08:13-07:00","id":166072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=165981#post165981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reminds me a lot of the False Awakening from nWoD Mage, though that was a deliberate parody of Mary Sue archetypes. In case you're not aware:<br /> <br /> The False Awakening starts with someone seemingly Awakening to a Watchtower from a Supernal Realm no one's ever heard of before, with a combination of Favored Arcana that never existed before. This person rapidly grows in power, gaining a dot in Gnosis <i>every week</i>, until they finally reach Gnosis 10 and EXPLODE, taking out a city block with them. In reality, the False Awakening is an Abyssal intruder that spreads from one target to another, but needs to be constantly hunted down lest they do some <i>real</i> damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, i remember those guys, great idea indeed, have to re-read them someday, always asked myself if it might be possible for a person suffering such a contamination to somehow contain or at least forestall the process. That might end up being even scarier as such an unprepared madman or woman of a mary sue mage wannabe actually shapes the abyssal contamination into some weird parody of a sixth tower.<br /> <br /> But back on the actual topic, that is Exalted, chosen of a Forbidden God like Han-tha or behemoths like Sayla the Yellow Wyrm, Mokrelus, Oliphem or Mostath could make for most potentially interesting antagonist and/or allies. Were Juggernaut a bit smarter i might experiment with the idea of it somehow stealing a monstrance and twisting one black exaltation into an exigence of its own, so that this agent of his might may seek some way to finally heal or finally finish him.<br /> <br /> As an aside, i can see how the existence of exigents and the Black Market of Exaltations could actually serve Bronze Faction interests and Immaculate Dogma about <b>the anathema</b> as mad sorcerers that <b>stole </b>the power of gods to serve their own egotistical interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-11-2014, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T10:17:45-07:00","id":166077,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it would be possible for an exigency to &quot;stack&quot; with an existing exaltation - probably a very screwed-up black-market one. I'm thinking mainly of a Venom and Carnage symbiote-type Exigency where it gives powers to those that don't have any and augments/twists the powers of those that already do, with a physical manifestation that one needs to wear or absorb to complete the binding process.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, it'd be similar to an Akuma, but would be much more of a free agent.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T12:07:48-07:00","id":166152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=165981#post165981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reminds me a lot of the False Awakening from nWoD Mage, though that was a deliberate parody of Mary Sue archetypes. In case you're not aware:<br /> <br /> The False Awakening starts with someone seemingly Awakening to a Watchtower from a Supernal Realm no one's ever heard of before, with a combination of Favored Arcana that never existed before. This person rapidly grows in power, gaining a dot in Gnosis <i>every week</i>, until they finally reach Gnosis 10 and EXPLODE, taking out a city block with them. In reality, the False Awakening is an Abyssal intruder that spreads from one target to another, but needs to be constantly hunted down lest they do some <i>real</i> damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ahaha, that's fantastic. I gave up on nwod mage early but I keep hearing about great shit published later on in the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T13:49:12-07:00","id":166209,"title":"","content":"The False Awakening was an inspiration, I admit.<br /> <br /> If you want to go a little less plummet-to-the-top, I think a hilarious chain of charms would be a set that improve your Stunts, a la (Yozi) Mythos Exultant, stacking and making your stunts <i>uber-awesome-shiny</i>...<br /> <br /> But each one restricts what kind of stunts gain a benefit. The starting charm might require that the Stunt includes the destruction of something, another one might refine that by requiring the stunt to also cause physical or emotional harm to others, still another might limit the minimum amount of harm your stunt can do...<br /> <br /> Until you are getting off easy Perfect effects by stunting... in exchange for each of your stunts being an <i>atrocity</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T21:49:53-07:00","id":166620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=165983#post165983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you provide stats for the thing, people will play as the thing. If you do not provide stats for the thing, people will make up their own stats and play as the thing anyway. This &quot;limited to NPC&quot; concept is strange and confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>People will try. As the ST, all I have to do is say &quot;no&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T00:50:27-07:00","id":166700,"title":"","content":"Shining Gear, god of Combat Automata, had fallen on hard times in the Second Age. Though he held a little hope that someone might rediscover the Bronze Legionnaire factory-cathedrals of Denandsor or the hidden thinking godstrider in the Far South, he knew that there was little possibility of recovery.<br /> <br /> Unlike many Celestial Gods who see their post as a stepping stone to greater power, Shining Gear was an ancient being created by Autochthon specifically to fill his role, and he held a deep, abiding love for his work. No longer able to bear the pain of his loss, he petitioned the Most High for an Exaltation, a champion with which the world might once again be reminded of the wonders he held dear. After much deliberation, he selected Maka, a young mechanist and engineer working on guild projects in the small Northern hub city of Hornhearth. He did not survive her ascension.<br /> <br /> Shining Gear has chosen both well and poorly. Maka immediately started correcting what she saw as decades of injustice against her genius. Using her Charms, she constructs increasingly more deadly fighting machines and directs them to rampage upon the city, destroying anyone who she can recall slighting her. So far, the coordinated efforts of the guard and a sworn brotherhood of Outcaste mercenaries have been able to thwart her, but they are reaching their limits, while the elusive Maka seems to have none. On the other hand, Hornhearth is certainly reminded of the purview of Shining Gear, and Guild-backed fanes fill his now-neglected alms cup with ambrosia and prayers for intervention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 06-12-2014, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T04:20:25-07:00","id":166842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=166620#post166620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People will try. As the ST, all I have to do is say &quot;no&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the GM, your power to change the game is only limited by your imagination and your group's willingness to put up with the changes you make.<br /> <br /> This has no bearing on game design, though. The author of the game can suggest how things should work, but can't effectively forbid anything. You can bet there are people somewhere playing gods, demons, Primordials and behemoths in Exalted, as well as people running around with resurrection and time travel magic, even though these things are either not officially supported or outright banned by the metaphysics of the setting.<br /> <br /> Presenting things as strictly NPC or, even worse, strictly antagonist territory has no place in the design paradigm of Exalted, because making something NPC only implies it cannot be reasoned or sympathized with, and that's something Exalted deliberately avoids. Worse, presenting something as just antagonists implies there is objective right and wrong in the setting, and that's antithetical to the kind of stories Exalted wants to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T05:08:16-07:00","id":166858,"title":"","content":"RoGD has tips for how to balance Spirit PCs against exalted ones because they knew damn well people were going to do it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T11:15:45-07:00","id":167093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=166077#post166077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it would be possible for an exigency to &quot;stack&quot; with an existing exaltation - probably a very screwed-up black-market one. I'm thinking mainly of a Venom and Carnage symbiote-type Exigency where it gives powers to those that don't have any and augments/twists the powers of those that already do, with a physical manifestation that one needs to wear or absorb to complete the binding process.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, it'd be similar to an Akuma, but would be much more of a free agent.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Something like an Akuma built into a demonic coadjutor, perharps? That could make a decent expy for the symbiot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=166858#post166858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RoGD has tips for how to balance Spirit PCs against exalted ones because they knew damn well people were going to do it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. Could you indicate the specific pages about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-12-2014, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T12:49:15-07:00","id":167146,"title":"","content":"It's right at the end of RoGd 1, pages 172 ad 173.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T13:04:00-07:00","id":167165,"title":"","content":"The chief reason to make something unplayable is that it alters the mechanical constraints you're operating under, which can allow you to make a more sleek and purpose-built NPC. Sometimes this seems worth it, sometimes not! Not everything human-ish has to resemble a playable character, but I definitely wouldn't design something that <i>did </i>look like a playable character and then tell everybody not to play it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T15:43:00-07:00","id":167295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=166842#post166842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As the GM, your power to change the game is only limited by your imagination and your group's willingness to put up with the changes you make. This has no bearing on game design, though. The author of the game can suggest how things should work, but can't effectively forbid anything. You can bet there are people somewhere playing gods, demons, Primordials and behemoths in Exalted, as well as people running around with resurrection and time travel magic, even though these things are either not officially supported or outright banned by the metaphysics of the setting. Presenting things as strictly NPC or, even worse, strictly antagonist territory has no place in the design paradigm of Exalted, because making something NPC only implies it cannot be reasoned or sympathized with, and that's something Exalted deliberately avoids. Worse, presenting something as just antagonists implies there is objective right and wrong in the setting, and that's antithetical to the kind of stories Exalted wants to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with you to a degree. Notice that i said that *I* was going to use them as NPC antagonists only, because the game i want to run is about solars, terrestrials, lunars and sidereals and occasionally an abyssal on the road to redemption. how everyone else whishes to run exalted is up to them. But i do disagree that restricting certain types of characters to NPC status is antithetical to the types of stories in Exalted. to me, exalted is about heroism, with everything implies (falls from grace, redemption, overcoming strife, hard decisions etc). i need neither exigent nor infernal PC's to tell the kinds of stories i like to tell. And i dont get offended if a player wants to bow out of a game i'm running because it's not the type of game he wants to play. i get that. i've bowed out of games for that very reason myself. to each their own, and mine includes neither exigent nor infernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":779,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","user":"NuSoardGraphite","date":". 06-13-2014, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T17:33:05-07:00","id":167368,"title":"","content":"I think the objection is about designing certain splats as NPC-only in the books. People are free to do whatever at their tables, but if Infernals or sidereals or whatever were <i>designed</i> as NPC-only, <i>everyone</i> is automatically &quot;bowed-out&quot; of games involving playing as those, with no option to &quot;bowing-in&quot; at a game that has them unless <b>massive </b>house-ruling is done to allow it.<br /> <br /> In other words, restricting certain types of characters to NPC/antagonist status <i>at your table</i> is fine. But <i>writing those splats that way in the books</i> is counterproductive to the intents of the game line, which is clearly intended to tell a broader range of stories than the particular brand of heroism you want in your games. Still, I'm talking mostly about mortals, Exalt types and other beings more or less or that scale (ghosts, Fair Folk, et cetera). Rules for playing as a &quot;Kaiju Behemoth* circle&quot; or rules for playing as a bunch of mundane animals are likely outside the intended scope of the game as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\">Especially since Behemoths is a catch-all term for a bunch of unrelated things, it doesn't really make sense to have &quot;Behemoth character&quot; rules</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T17:43:30-07:00","id":167377,"title":"","content":"I don't like the &quot;Exaltation Symbiote&quot; idea for a few reasons - for one, the symbiotes in the Marvel universe are capable of finding other hosts without killing the original bearer. In fact, Venom is Venom <i>because the symbiote separated from Peter Parker</i>. Also, the symbiotes had ways of being neutralized temporarily (or even eradicated permanently!) in ways that rendered the host pretty much an ordinary schlub. Additionally, we already <i>have</i> a demon that acts as an amorphous mass that can bond with a host and protect said host from danger.<br /> <br /> Also, if something can empower a person who's already Exalted and can depart from said host prematurely, that flies in the face of what little we know about Exaltation. While I'm in favor of shaking up some assumptions set in the game, the notion of an Exaltation that can be taken away, well, let's just say I'm against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T18:05:55-07:00","id":167387,"title":"","content":"I think the symbiote thing would be better represented as an artifact with an MI that can learn it's own evocations and can deattune itself or force the attunement to be held<br /> <br /> <br /> back on topic though, I wonder what an exigent of the god of keys would look like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T19:31:55-07:00","id":167433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=167387#post167387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the symbiote thing would be better represented as an artifact with an MI that can learn it's own evocations and can deattune itself or force the attunement to be held</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, but i just went along with what was asked/suggested.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=167387#post167387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">back on topic though, I wonder what an exigent of the god of keys would look like</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, i would probably wonder about what would the god of keys would look like first.<br /> <br /> Would like to see some sample exigents and their charms just to get into the right &quot;making stuff up&quot; mindset too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T19:32:23-07:00","id":167434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=167387#post167387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the symbiote thing would be better represented as an artifact with an MI that can learn it's own evocations and can deattune itself or force the attunement to be held<br /> <br /> <br /> back on topic though, I wonder what an exigent of the god of keys would look like</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably, something like this:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://72.10.171.98/resources/ecommerce/images/products/590/124/img124590/product-enlarged.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> More seriously I'd imagine a character whose fighting style involves throwing keys like perfect knives and not actually dealing damage - the keys enter the skin and lock whichever bodypart they landed on in that position (and maybe in that exact spot, as though they were pinned to an invisible wall).<br /> <br /> It could depend on the paradigm too - one key that fits all locks could imply a small amount of shapeshifting or adaptation; having every key for every lock could imply pulling a lot of things out at just the right time (&quot;I have the key to the mystery / the problem / the conundrum / solving the conflict&quot;). I can depend on just how heavily you want to abuse the &quot;key&quot; and &quot;lock&quot; metaphors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T19:33:30-07:00","id":167435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=167387#post167387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">back on topic though, I wonder what an exigent of the god of keys would look like</div> </div> </div> </div>I bet they'd be really good at convincing their lovers to agree to an open relationship","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T19:35:51-07:00","id":167436,"title":"","content":"Ever read Neverwhere?<br /> <br /> Door was an Exigent to the God of Keys.<br /> <br /> Her family's magic is that they could open <i>anything.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T19:36:24-07:00","id":167437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=167387#post167387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">back on topic though, I wonder what an exigent of the god of keys would look like</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, I like this. You could do a hell of a lot with this concept. Just to get the obvious issue out of the way first, though: no keyblades. It's not that I think keyblades are too dumb for exalted, or anything, it's just...a little too on the nose.<br /> <br /> I think the thematic essence of keys is that they allow you to make something difficult or impossible on purpose (as a deterrent), while still keeping it trivial for a select few. A key is the thing that puts you on the happy side of a filter. In fiction, a key is usually a &quot;win button&quot; to a single specific challenge (opening something, usually but sometimes also turning on a computer, or bossing around an automaton, or whatever). Thus, you've effectively overcome that challenge when you get the key, and the suspense factor is in whether you're able to do so. This, along with the fact that keys tend to do a very specific narrow thing (this key opens <i>this</i> door), are what I think is their conceptual &quot;core&quot;.<br /> <br /> In that vein, I see an Exigent of Keys having a lot of powers that allow them to completely steamroll or circumvent obstacles, but that require a lot of work to set up, or require them to &quot;find&quot; something, or something like that. Not a lot of powers that work in a straightforward way out-of-box, but once they find the &quot;key&quot; for a single highly specific thing, they have recourse to it in the future and can perhaps &quot;lend it&quot; to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 06-12-2014, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T20:11:10-07:00","id":167448,"title":"","content":"And when your key *doesn't* fit the lock you're trying to open, you can always call the locksmith <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T00:12:45-07:00","id":169545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/165354-monster-of-the-week-exigency?p=167437#post167437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh, I like this. You could do a hell of a lot with this concept. Just to get the obvious issue out of the way first, though: no keyblades. It's not that I think keyblades are too dumb for exalted, or anything, it's just...a little too on the nose.<br /> <br /> I think the thematic essence of keys is that they allow you to make something difficult or impossible on purpose (as a deterrent), while still keeping it trivial for a select few. A key is the thing that puts you on the happy side of a filter. In fiction, a key is usually a &quot;win button&quot; to a single specific challenge (opening something, usually but sometimes also turning on a computer, or bossing around an automaton, or whatever). Thus, you've effectively overcome that challenge when you get the key, and the suspense factor is in whether you're able to do so. This, along with the fact that keys tend to do a very specific narrow thing (this key opens <i>this</i> door), are what I think is their conceptual &quot;core&quot;.<br /> <br /> In that vein, I see an Exigent of Keys having a lot of powers that allow them to completely steamroll or circumvent obstacles, but that require a lot of work to set up, or require them to &quot;find&quot; something, or something like that. Not a lot of powers that work in a straightforward way out-of-box, but once they find the &quot;key&quot; for a single highly specific thing, they have recourse to it in the future and can perhaps &quot;lend it&quot; to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the thing about keys is that they can <b>close</b> things as much as they open them, what in itself sort of offers two directions to explore, mix-&amp;-match.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}